rk in 1837  although Ariel's story has changed  tremendously over the years one thing  remains the same area was willing to do  anything to shed her mermaid fins and  gain a human soul Andersen chose to take  a very tragic story and give it a happy  ending which totally caught Disney's  attention Walt Disney Animation Studios  rewrote Andersen story and published an  animated film with the same name in 1989  although Snow White and Cinderella might  be the most well-known fairy tales in  the world Ariel is by far one of the  most beloved Disney Princesses ever did  you guys know that there's a statue of  the original Ariel in Copenhagen Denmark  it's definitely something to check out  if you ever travel to that part of the  world and you'll win first prize at the  fair  tomorrow and become a world-famous  inventor Belle Princess Belle is an  intelligent and brave seventeen year old  woman whose towel is literally as old as  time  it's believed that her story was written  in the second century in fact some  fanatics believe Beauty and the Beast to  be the first fairy tale ever created  however the first draft of this story  was published by Gabrielle Susan de vil  louvet in 1740 the world as we know it  believes that Belle's origins are rooted  in France much like Cinderella and  Aurora's Gabrielle Suzanne's original  work was over a hundred pages long and  told a very different tale than the one  were familiar with in 1757 author Marie  lip prints de Beaumont shortens and  revamped gabrielle Suzanne's story  making it more child-friendly and over  two centuries later Disney chose to  animate Belle's fairy tale and turn it  into the masterpiece it is today  although we might have met Disney's  Belle in 1991 her story has allegedly  been around for thousands of years  Pocahontas many of us know Pocahontas as  the eighteen-year-old Disney Princess  who chose to listen to her heart instead  of her head the world first met her in  1995 when the Disney classic Pocahontas 